{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>As has been done this day, HaShem commanded to do, to make atonement for you.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in tractate Yoma chapter 1: 'As has been done this day' — this is the eighth day of consecration, for which you keep seven days before it; so too 'HaShem commanded to do' — this is the matter of the red heifer, that you must keep seven days before the burning of the heifer, by a gezerah shavah of צוה צוה: it is written here ״צוה ה' לעשות,״ and it is written concerning the heifer (Numbers 19): ״זאת חקת התורה אשר צוה ה'.״ 'To make atonement for you' — this is the matter of the Day of Atonement, that the High Priest separates seven days before the Day of Atonement. And that is what we learned: 'Seven days before the Day of Atonement they separate the High Priest from his house to the Chamber of Parhedrin'; and we also learned: 'Seven days before the burning of the heifer they separate the priest who burns the heifer from his house to the chamber that faces the Temple mount.' And this is the meaning of the verse: 'As has been done this day,' that there are seven days before it, so too HaShem commanded to do for the heifer seven days before its burning, and likewise 'to make atonement for you' — that is the Day of Atonement, for which the High Priest separates seven days before it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:05.889489185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}